routes.realism:
The most photographic plants available in a browser, because they are photographs (examples: https://omolism.cargo.site/SplatGarden, https://nebulousflynn.substack.com/p/3d-gaussian-splats-of-local-flora).

But the lighting is baked from the capture day. They:
- cannot follow DeckCraft's sun, time of day or night look;
- cast no shadows without proxy casters;
- show fuzzy edges close up;
- are not traced by three-gpu-pathtracer.

Relighting is a research topic (https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.20512).
